# Applied Energistics 2 – the book "AE2 Basics"
# File ae2guide.lang -> key prefix 'ae2guide.'

item.name = AE2 Basics
item.description = A handbook for getting started with Applied Energistics 2: every step and all Inscriber recipes, with pictures. Right or left click to open it.

book.title = AE2 Basics
book.subtitle = Your first steps with Applied Energistics 2
book.intro = Store thousands of items in a few blocks and let your base craft for you. This book takes you from the first workbench to your first ME network. Pick a chapter on the right or turn the pages with the arrows below.
book.contents = Contents
book.contentsButton = Contents

workbench.title = The Energistics Workbench
workbench.text1 = Every AE2 recipe is crafted at the Energistics Workbench. You build it at a normal Workbench, in the Tinkering category.
workbench.text2 = You need 8 iron bars, 6 copper bars, 4 white crystals and 4 tree trunks. Place it somewhere central – you will come back to it all the time.

meteorite.title = Meteorites
meteorite.text1 = AE2 has no ores. Certus quartz, sky stone and the four inscriber presses come from meteorites: craters with a body of sky stone and a small chamber in the middle. Charge an iron bar in the Charger to get a Meteorite Compass – it points to the nearest meteorite.
meteorite.text2 = Mine the Mysterious Cube in the middle of the meteorite: it drops all four presses. You only need each press once – the Inscriber keeps it and can copy it.
meteorite.text3 = Meteorites only appear in terrain that was generated after the mod was installed. For older worlds the Energistics Workbench has fallback recipes for the presses, sky stone and certus quartz.

quartz.title = Growing Certus Quartz
quartz.text1 = Budding certus quartz from a meteorite grows buds on all free sides: small, medium and large buds, then a cluster. Mine the cluster for certus quartz crystals; smaller buds only drop dust. Flawed, chipped and damaged budding quartz wear out while growing, flawless budding quartz lasts forever – so do not break it.
quartz.text2 = A powered Growth Accelerator next to the budding quartz makes it grow much faster. Certus Quartz Dust comes from the Inscriber and is smelted into Silicon in a furnace.

charger.title = The Charger
charger.text1 = Put a certus quartz crystal into the Charger to turn it into a Charged Certus Quartz Crystal. The Charger needs power: connect it to an ME network or place a Crank on it and turn it by hand.
charger.text2 = The Charger also fills the batteries of the Wireless Terminal, portable cells and the powered tools.

fluix.title = Fluix Crystals
fluix.text1 = Throw a Charged Certus Quartz Crystal, a red crystal and a white crystal together into water. After a few seconds they turn into two Fluix Crystals – the material of cables and most ME devices.
fluix.text2 = The same way a Charged Certus Quartz Crystal and Certus Quartz Dust grow into two new certus crystals, and a quartz block becomes budding quartz again.

inscriber.title = The Inscriber
inscriber.text1 = The Inscriber has three slots: a press on top, the material in the middle and a press or a second material at the bottom. Power it with a Crank or from the network. Sneak and use it to install Acceleration Cards.
inscriber.text2 = Processors are made in three steps: press a printed circuit with its press, press Printed Silicon with the Silicon Press, then put both together with a red crystal in the middle.
inscriber.text3 = Presses stay in the Inscriber and are never used up. With a press on top and an iron bar in the middle the Inscriber makes a copy of the press.
inscriber.text4 = Right click with a Cutting Knife to cut a Name Press. In the top or bottom slot of the Inscriber it gives the item in the middle a new name.
