power.title = Power
power.text1 = ME networks run on AE energy. The Vibration Chamber burns fuel such as wood or charcoal, the Crystal Resonance Generator produces a little energy all the time without fuel.
power.text2 = Energy Cells store energy for your network. Look at any AE2 block to see the energy, channels and usage of its network.

network.title = Your first ME network
network.text1 = Place an ME Drive, put a storage cell into it and connect an ME Terminal with cables. Cables connect to their neighbours on their own; coloured cables only connect to the same colour or fluix.
network.text2 = Open the terminal to store and take items. Everything in the drive's cells shows up there, and the cell tooltip tells you how full a cell is.
network.text3 = Without a controller a network can use 8 channels. For more devices build an ME Controller; normal cables carry 8 channels, dense cables 32.

autocrafting.title = Autocrafting
autocrafting.text1 = The Pattern Encoding Terminal turns a recipe and a Blank Pattern into an encoded pattern. Put the pattern into a Pattern Provider next to a Molecular Assembler or a machine.
autocrafting.text2 = Build a Crafting CPU from crafting units and crafting storage. Then you can request any item with a pattern in the terminal, and the network crafts it for you.

tips.title = Tips
tips.text1 = Sneak and use a machine, bus or Pattern Provider to install upgrade cards and change its settings.
tips.text2 = The Wrench rotates devices and dismantles them when you sneak, the Network Tool shows the status of a network, and the Memory Card copies settings from one device to another.
tips.text3 = Every AE2 item explains in its description what it does. Type /ae2 language de to switch AE2 to German.
